---
title: "This Page Needs Different Permissions"
permalink: "/session-refresh/index.html"
layout: page
---
<p>
  You're signed in, but this page isn't available with your current permissions.
  The most common cause is a sign-in that predates a change to your access, which
  signing in again fixes.
</p>

<p>
  <a href="/.auth/logout?post_logout_redirect_uri=/admin/">Sign in again and return to the editor</a>
</p>

<p>
  If you were looking for member resources rather than the website editor, go to
  <a href="/members/">the members area</a> instead.
</p>

<p>
  If signing in again brings you back here, contact an administrator rather than
  assuming the problem is your account. It may be that you aren't assigned to the
  website editor app, but the site returns this same page when it can't verify
  permissions at all &mdash; for example if its Microsoft&nbsp;365 credentials have
  expired. Those need different fixes, and only the server logs tell them apart.
</p>
